# Fixed defect 131, 2026-09-28, the one place a failed head says nothing about
# its body. Symptom: `if (n > 0` over `y = 3 )` cost `expected_group_close`
# and then `missing_body` at the next statement, and that statement's own
# mistake was dropped. Cause: the group runs to the first `)` it can close
# with, the body's own, so the body line went into the head; its absence is
# the recovery's doing, not the author's, and naming it names the first
# mistake again. A head whose recovery ran past its own line says nothing
# about a body it did not find (`parse/opening`), and the statement below it
# is read.
#
# Widened 2026-10-02 (lane recovery-b8, the head class, the audit's row
# 130-34d): the `)` at the body line's end, one too many, which paired the
# group, is told too. The lines from the head's to that closer are the
# body, read as one (`parse/swallowed`), and the closer is its junk.

function unclosed(n: i64)
    if (n > 0
        y = 3 )  #~ expected_group_close expected_end_of_line
    z = 4 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)
